// OpenWar3 override — `UI\FrameDef\Glue\GameChatroom.fdf` (the game lobby).
//
// Where the other players type to reach this game — the other half of the LAN screen's
// "Join by address" field (src/overrides/ui/LocalMultiplayerJoin.fdf).
//
// Real WC3 needed neither: it broadcast, and a game on the network simply appeared in the
// list. We cannot broadcast from a page, and the packaged game has no address bar to navigate
// with, so the host has to be able to READ its own address and the joiner to type it. This is
// the reading half, and it belongs here rather than on the screen before it: an address is
// worth passing on only once there is a game at it.
//
// The value is CLICKED to copy — there is no button because the game's smallest button chrome
// is a fifth of the panel wide, and a row of text that copies itself is the smaller thing on a
// column already carrying the map and the options summary. The label says so; nothing here is
// discoverable by hovering.
//
// It sits in the BAND BETWEEN THE TWO PANELS at the bottom of the screen, not in the map column
// above the buttons where it started. That band is empty at every aspect the game is actually
// played at, so the row costs the screen nothing, and it reads as what it is — a note about this
// machine rather than another line of the map's summary.
//
// Anchored to the RIGHT panel's own button backdrop rather than to the screen: the gap exists
// because the button column is anchored to the right edge and the chat panel to the left, so
// hanging off the column's edge keeps the row in the gap as the gap moves. Anchoring it to the
// root's centre with a fixed offset would drift the moment the window is not 16:9.
//
// Both frames state a Height because our solver does not size a TEXT to its string the way the
// engine does, and both are as WIDE AS THE BAND ITSELF and centred in it: the frame's right edge
// is the button column's left edge and its width is the gap, so JUSTIFYCENTER puts the line on
// the band's own middle rather than against one of its sides.

Frame "TEXT" "JoinAddressLobbyLabel" INHERITS "StandardLabelTextTemplate" {
    Width 0.235,
    Height 0.012,
    SetPoint BOTTOMRIGHT, "CancelBackdrop", BOTTOMLEFT, 0.0, 0.040,
    FontJustificationH JUSTIFYCENTER,
}

Frame "TEXT" "JoinAddressLobbyValue" INHERITS "StandardValueTextTemplate" {
    Width 0.235,
    Height 0.012,
    SetPoint TOPRIGHT, "JoinAddressLobbyLabel", BOTTOMRIGHT, 0.0, -0.002,
    FontJustificationH JUSTIFYCENTER,
}
